    "source_label": "Application activity 3.15 (Unit 9), question 2b",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "prompt": {
      "text": "For the same distribution (x = 2, 4, 6 with P(X = x) = a, 2a² − a, a² + a − 1), find E(X), exactly or to three decimal places.",
      "tex": "\\begin{array}{c|ccc} x & 2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ \\hline P(X = x) & a & 2a^2 - a & a^2 + a - 1 \\end{array}"
    },
    "answer": {
      "check": "numeric",
      "expected": "26/9",
      "check_args": {
        "tolerance": 0.001
      },
      "accepted": [
        "26/9",
        "2.889",
        "E(X) = 26/9"
      ],
      "display_tex": "E(X) = \\frac{26}{9}",
      "input": "expression"
    },
    "hints": [
      "First find a from the condition that the probabilities add up to 1 (the previous exercise): a = 2/3.",
      "With a = 2/3 the probabilities of 2, 4 and 6 are 2/3, 2/9 and 1/9.",
      "E(X) = 2(2/3) + 4(2/9) + 6(1/9). Add the fractions."
    ],
    "solution": [
      {
        "text": "With a = 2/3 the probabilities are:",
        "tex": "P(X = 2) = \\frac{2}{3}, \\quad P(X = 4) = \\frac{2}{9}, \\quad P(X = 6) = \\frac{1}{9}"
      },
      {
        "text": "Multiply each value by its probability and add.",
        "tex": "E(X) = 2\\cdot\\frac{2}{3} + 4\\cdot\\frac{2}{9} + 6\\cdot\\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{12}{9} + \\frac{8}{9} + \\frac{6}{9} = \\frac{26}{9}"
      }
    ],
