    "source_label": "Application activity 3.15 (Unit 9), question 3",
    "difficulty": "intermediate",
    "prompt": {
      "text": "A fair die is thrown once and X is the score. Find the standard deviation of X, correct to two decimal places.",
      "tex": "X \\in \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\}, \\qquad P(X = x) = \\frac{1}{6}"
    },
    "answer": {
      "check": "numeric",
      "expected": "sqrt(35/12)",
      "check_args": {
        "tolerance": 0.006
      },
      "accepted": [
        "1.71",
        "sqrt(35/12)",
        "SD(X) = 1.71"
      ],
      "display_tex": "SD(X) = \\sqrt{\\frac{35}{12}} \\approx 1.71",
      "input": "expression"
    },
    "hints": [
      "Each score 1 to 6 has probability 1/6. Find E(X) and E(X²) first.",
      "E(X) = 21/6 = 3.5 and E(X²) = (1 + 4 + 9 + 16 + 25 + 36)/6 = 91/6.",
      "Var(X) = 91/6 − 3.5² = 35/12. Take the square root."
    ],
    "solution": [
      {
        "text": "Expected value.",
        "tex": "E(X) = \\frac{1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6}{6} = \\frac{21}{6} = 3.5"
      },
      {
        "text": "Expectation of X².",
        "tex": "E(X^2) = \\frac{1 + 4 + 9 + 16 + 25 + 36}{6} = \\frac{91}{6}"
      },
      {
        "text": "Variance.",
        "tex": "\\operatorname{Var}(X) = \\frac{91}{6} - (3.5)^2 = \\frac{91}{6} - \\frac{49}{4} = \\frac{35}{12}"
      },
      {
        "text": "Standard deviation.",
        "tex": "SD(X) = \\sqrt{\\frac{35}{12}} \\approx 1.71"
      }
    ],
    "review": {
      "status": "developer-test",
      "reviewed_by": null,
      "date": null
    }
  }
